        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Figures of speech are departures from ordinary language use — ways of arranging words (schemes) or substituting meanings (tropes) that produce emphasis, beauty, emotional force, or memorable expression. Classical rhetoric catalogued hundreds of figures; this guide covers the most important ones with definitions, examples, and practical effects."
